WEBVTT

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Now that's my little Margie. I've been both mother and father to her since she was born.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.000
She's grown up now and you think my job's all done, eh? Well, that's what you think.

00:40.000 --> 00:44.000
When she was little I could spank her and make her mind me. I had control over her.

00:44.000 --> 00:47.000
I made her eat her spinach. No candy before meals.

00:47.000 --> 00:51.000
And when she disobeyed I took her roller skates away for a week.

00:51.000 --> 00:55.000
But what can you do when a girl reaches this age? She's completely out of hand.

00:55.000 --> 01:00.000
I've got a problem, believe me. I've got a problem.

01:05.000 --> 01:11.000
That's my father. I've raised him from childhood. That is, my childhood.

01:11.000 --> 01:15.000
He's nearly 50 now and you'd think he'd settle down, wouldn't you?

01:15.000 --> 01:17.000
Well, that's what you think.

01:17.000 --> 01:22.000
Today he looks better in shorts on a tennis court than fellas 25.

01:22.000 --> 01:27.000
Girls wink at him and what's worse, he winks back at them.

01:27.000 --> 01:31.000
I want a nice old comfortable father.

01:31.000 --> 01:35.000
I try to look after him but he just won't settle down.

01:35.000 --> 02:00.000
I've got a problem, believe me. I've got a problem.

02:00.000 --> 02:02.000
Hold it a second, Charlie. I'll be right with you.

02:02.000 --> 02:05.000
Yes, sir. We may as well say good night here. There's no use asking for trouble.

02:05.000 --> 02:08.000
All right.

02:24.000 --> 02:28.000
You'll have to kiss me like that more often.

02:28.000 --> 02:30.000
Oh, excuse me.

02:30.000 --> 02:32.000
Hey, wait for me.

02:32.000 --> 02:35.000
Well, looks like you're stuck for another good night kiss. Come on, walk me to the door.

02:35.000 --> 02:36.000
What about your father?

02:36.000 --> 02:37.000
Oh, we'll be quiet.

02:37.000 --> 02:41.000
You know, every time your father approaches me, I automatically fondle my blue cross card.

02:41.000 --> 02:43.000
He's all talk. He wouldn't hurt you.

02:43.000 --> 02:47.000
All talk? You mean like last night when he talked a three-inch rip down the back of my tweed jacket?

02:47.000 --> 02:50.000
Well, considering it was nearly 2 a.m., a three-inch rip isn't bad.

02:50.000 --> 02:53.000
No, it was a nice little rip for 2 a.m.

02:53.000 --> 02:55.000
Sometime I'll have to try one of his 5 a.m. specials.

02:55.000 --> 02:58.000
They go all the way down the jacket, one trouser leg,

02:58.000 --> 03:02.000
and in good weather you can watch your argyle separate in a brilliant spectacle of color.

03:02.000 --> 03:04.000
Oh, Freddy, stop talking and kiss me good night again.

03:04.000 --> 03:07.000
Nothing like a good night kiss.

03:07.000 --> 03:08.000
Come on in.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.000
But your father.

03:09.000 --> 03:11.000
Oh, didn't I tell you? He's out for the evening.

03:11.000 --> 03:13.000
He's out? Well, why didn't you tell me?

03:13.000 --> 03:16.000
Well, it's like you said, Freddy. There's nothing like a good night kiss.

03:16.000 --> 03:19.000
When a fellow's sure it's his last kiss, he puts everything he's got into it.

03:19.000 --> 03:23.000
And the way I've worked it, we've already had two last kisses and still have one to go.

03:23.000 --> 03:25.000
Come on, I'll whip us up a snack.

03:25.000 --> 03:27.000
Are you positive about your father? It's nearly midnight.

03:27.000 --> 03:31.000
Will you stop worrying? Dad won't be home before 3 or 4, maybe later.

03:31.000 --> 03:32.000
Where'd he go?

03:32.000 --> 03:35.000
He took Roberta to the opening of the new Angio Piazza show.

03:35.000 --> 03:38.000
Oh, but that's over by now. No show runs this late.

03:38.000 --> 03:39.000
Look, I'd better be going.

03:39.000 --> 03:41.000
Don't be silly. I said he took Roberta.

03:41.000 --> 03:44.000
You know what that means. They won't be in till all hours.

03:44.000 --> 03:46.000
I've got to do something about her.

03:46.000 --> 03:47.000
I thought you liked Roberta.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.000
Sure, I like her, for anybody but Dad.

03:49.000 --> 03:53.000
Every time he takes her out, he thinks he has to do the town like some college boy.

03:53.000 --> 03:56.000
He's too old to be out dancing half the night.

03:56.000 --> 03:58.000
He ought to be home in bed.

03:58.000 --> 04:00.000
He'd look kind of silly dancing in bed.

04:00.000 --> 04:02.000
Freddy, it isn't a joke to me.

04:02.000 --> 04:05.000
Dad's nearly 50, but reminding him of it only makes him more stubborn.

04:05.000 --> 04:08.000
I wish Roberta would fall for somebody else.

04:08.000 --> 04:12.000
You could always toss some handsome guy her way. Get her married off.

04:12.000 --> 04:15.000
You may think that's funny, but I've seriously considered it.

04:15.000 --> 04:17.000
Trouble is, Roberta's so darn picky.

04:17.000 --> 04:19.000
She wouldn't go for just anybody.

04:19.000 --> 04:23.000
It'd have to be somebody really special to beat Dad in time.

04:23.000 --> 04:25.000
I wonder how Piazza's new show is.

04:25.000 --> 04:26.000
He's always great.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.000
Yeah, terrific guy.

04:28.000 --> 04:29.000
You like him?

04:29.000 --> 04:32.000
I thought most men hated him because they're envious of his good looks.

04:32.000 --> 04:33.000
You want to know something?

04:33.000 --> 04:34.000
What?

04:34.000 --> 04:37.000
If Piazza ever saw you, he'd envy me.

04:37.000 --> 04:39.000
Just for that, I'll give you a choice.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.000
Cheese on rye or cheese on white?

04:41.000 --> 04:43.000
How about a slice of both, huh?

04:51.000 --> 04:53.000
What's that for?

04:53.000 --> 04:54.000
Just in case.

04:54.000 --> 04:55.000
Freddy, will you relax?

04:55.000 --> 04:58.000
I told you Dad won't be home for hours.

04:58.000 --> 05:00.000
I'm sorry, but I just don't agree with you.

05:00.000 --> 05:02.000
Just a second. We'll let Charlie give us his opinion.

05:02.000 --> 05:04.000
But Vern, it's such a silly thing to argue about, darling.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.000
It's not that important.

05:06.000 --> 05:08.000
Of course it isn't, but it won't hurt to prove that I'm right.

05:08.000 --> 05:10.000
Now, Charlie, give me your honest opinion.

05:10.000 --> 05:11.000
What do you think of Angio Piazza?

05:11.000 --> 05:12.000
You've seen him, haven't you?

05:12.000 --> 05:15.000
Not on the stage, but I caught him in a couple television shows.

05:15.000 --> 05:17.000
Okay, now tell me what you think of him.

05:17.000 --> 05:19.000
Don't let me influence you, but just say what you think.

05:19.000 --> 05:23.000
I'll be very surprised if a man of your intelligence doesn't agree a thousand percent

05:23.000 --> 05:27.000
that Piazza's a stuffy, sticky ham and not too handsome either.

05:27.000 --> 05:29.000
Gee, Miss Talbright, I'd like to go along with you,

05:29.000 --> 05:31.000
but I think the guy's got something.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.000
Why, if I had a face like his and all the girls would be swimming over me...

05:34.000 --> 05:36.000
All right, Charles, all right.

05:36.000 --> 05:38.000
You're not mad at me, are you, sir?

05:38.000 --> 05:40.000
You're entitled to your own opinion.

05:40.000 --> 05:41.000
But you didn't say good night.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.000
Good night.

05:42.000 --> 05:43.000
Good night.

05:43.000 --> 05:45.000
You're coming in for nightcap, aren't you?

05:45.000 --> 05:47.000
Well, from your general attitude, I thought you'd cancel the invitation.

05:47.000 --> 05:49.000
Oh, Roberta dear, let's not be childish.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
Let's forget about the whole thing, okay?

05:51.000 --> 05:54.000
Okay.

05:54.000 --> 06:00.000
I'll get some more meth.

06:00.000 --> 06:01.000
Guess who?

06:01.000 --> 06:04.000
Give me a hand, kid.

06:04.000 --> 06:09.000
Sit down, dear. I'll get some ice.

06:09.000 --> 06:12.000
Still can't guess.

06:12.000 --> 06:14.000
Give me another clue. I think I'm getting warm.

06:14.000 --> 06:18.000
I'll give you a real clue.

06:18.000 --> 06:20.000
Margie, where are your hands?

06:20.000 --> 06:21.000
I'm here, why?

06:21.000 --> 06:23.000
I think we have company.

06:23.000 --> 06:24.000
Guess who?

06:24.000 --> 06:26.000
I was just about to leave, Mr. Albright.

06:26.000 --> 06:28.000
Now, Dad, take it easy. Think of your health.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.000
Think of my health.

06:29.000 --> 06:30.000
Leave me alone with Freddie just a minute, dear.

06:30.000 --> 06:31.000
But, Dad...

06:31.000 --> 06:33.000
Don't worry. There won't be any trouble.

06:33.000 --> 06:38.000
All right.

06:38.000 --> 06:40.000
Relax, Freddie.

06:40.000 --> 06:42.000
I just want to ask you a simple question.

06:42.000 --> 06:44.000
Sure, sure, Mr. Albright.

06:44.000 --> 06:47.000
Now, here's the deal.

06:47.000 --> 06:51.000
I know how Margie feels about a certain party, so I'm not going to bother asking her.

06:51.000 --> 06:54.000
But you see, Miss Townsend and I had a slight disagreement tonight.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.000
And although I don't mind losing an argument once in a while,

06:56.000 --> 06:58.000
I do like to feel that there's somebody on my side.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.000
Do you follow me?

06:59.000 --> 07:01.000
Not at all. But whatever it is, sir, I'm on your side.

07:01.000 --> 07:03.000
Good, good.

07:03.000 --> 07:06.000
You know, somehow I don't recall coming in here and seeing you kissing Margie.

07:06.000 --> 07:07.000
Swell!

07:07.000 --> 07:09.000
Now, what's the lie you want me to tell?

07:09.000 --> 07:12.000
Well, Roberta and I saw a play tonight.

07:12.000 --> 07:15.000
And then he became so infuriated, we left the Copa without even dancing once.

07:15.000 --> 07:18.000
Just because the waiter said he liked Angiopiasa?

07:18.000 --> 07:22.000
Oh, don't. That name is poison to your father, as of right now.

07:22.000 --> 07:28.000
But he'll get over it.

07:28.000 --> 07:29.000
Roberta, my dear.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.000
Yes, Vern.

07:30.000 --> 07:31.000
About Angiopiasa.

07:31.000 --> 07:33.000
Oh, Vern, no more tonight, please.

07:33.000 --> 07:35.000
But dear, I thought it would be kind of nice to hear what Freddie has to say.

07:35.000 --> 07:37.000
No, Freddie. Don't say anything.

07:37.000 --> 07:39.000
Why not? I'm entitled to an opinion.

07:39.000 --> 07:41.000
Go home, Freddie. Go now.

07:41.000 --> 07:42.000
Don't say a word.

07:42.000 --> 07:43.000
Margie, please.

07:43.000 --> 07:46.000
What do you say, Freddie? What do you think of Angiopiasa?

07:46.000 --> 07:47.000
I think he's a bum.

07:47.000 --> 07:49.000
Strictly a no-talent bum.

07:49.000 --> 07:51.000
Kind of goony, too.

07:51.000 --> 07:52.000
Well, Roberta, dear.

07:52.000 --> 07:55.000
Vern Albright, I've had just about all of this that I can stand for one evening.

07:55.000 --> 07:58.000
I've seen you in childish moods before, but never quite so ridiculous.

07:58.000 --> 08:02.000
I like Angiopiasa, and I plan to keep right on liking him.

08:02.000 --> 08:05.000
I think he's perfectly charming and extremely handsome.

08:05.000 --> 08:08.000
We can't all have an Angiopiasa, but we can dream.

08:08.000 --> 08:10.000
Put that under your pillow and sleep on it.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
Good night.

08:12.000 --> 08:15.000
Wait, Roberta.

08:15.000 --> 08:17.000
You and your big mouth.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.000
But, Mr. Albright.

08:18.000 --> 08:23.000
Go home.

08:23.000 --> 08:25.000
And don't come back.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.000
Freddie.

08:26.000 --> 08:28.000
Margie, this place confuses me.

08:28.000 --> 08:29.000
It confuses me.

08:29.000 --> 08:30.000
I'm sorry.

08:30.000 --> 08:33.000
But listen, remember what we were talking about, about marrying Roberta off?

08:33.000 --> 08:35.000
Margie, you're getting that look in your eye.

08:35.000 --> 08:36.000
Good night.

08:36.000 --> 08:37.000
Oh, Freddie, wait.

08:37.000 --> 08:38.000
You heard it yourself.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.000
She's crazy about Angiopiasa.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.000
Margie, look.

08:41.000 --> 08:43.000
You've done some of the craziest things I've ever heard of.

08:43.000 --> 08:48.000
But if you think you can get to the biggest star of the season, honey, it's impossible.

08:48.000 --> 08:49.000
Well, there must be some way, Freddie.

08:49.000 --> 08:50.000
Think of something.

08:50.000 --> 08:52.000
Oh, stop dreaming, baby.

08:52.000 --> 08:53.000
There isn't a chance.

08:53.000 --> 08:58.000
Well, the guy doesn't even answer his telephone unless it's Morton Warnock or some big producer like that calling.

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
Morton Warnock?

09:00.000 --> 09:01.000
You're getting that look again.

09:01.000 --> 09:03.000
It just might work.

09:03.000 --> 09:04.000
Margie, the elevator's coming.

09:04.000 --> 09:05.000
Kiss me good night.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.000
I'm sure it'll work.

09:07.000 --> 09:14.000
Good night, Margie.

09:14.000 --> 09:15.000
Yes, that's right.

09:15.000 --> 09:19.000
May I speak with him, please?

09:19.000 --> 09:21.000
Mr. Morton Warnock's secretary, Mr. Piazza.

09:21.000 --> 09:22.000
He's the producer, sir.

09:22.000 --> 09:24.000
Who cares about him?

09:24.000 --> 09:26.000
She's a lady young and beautiful.

09:26.000 --> 09:28.000
Oh, she sounds young.

09:28.000 --> 09:30.000
Then she must be beautiful.

09:30.000 --> 09:32.000
I shall insist upon it.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.000
Angiopiasa speaking.

09:34.000 --> 09:35.000
Mr. Piazza?

09:35.000 --> 09:41.000
Mr. Warnock is giving a little cocktail party today at 5, and he'd like very much to have you come.

09:41.000 --> 09:45.000
I won't be able to stay very long, but I shall be delighted to drop in.

09:45.000 --> 09:49.000
She's a vision.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.000
Yes?

09:50.000 --> 09:52.000
Angiopiasa's secretary.

09:52.000 --> 09:53.000
Angiopiasa's secretary.

09:53.000 --> 09:56.000
Put her on.

09:56.000 --> 09:57.000
Hello?

09:57.000 --> 09:58.000
Mr. Warnock?

09:58.000 --> 10:04.000
Mr. Piazza's giving a little cocktail party today at 5, and he'd like very much to have you come.

10:04.000 --> 10:06.000
Margie, are you serious?

10:06.000 --> 10:08.000
How did you ever manage to get him to...

10:08.000 --> 10:10.000
Oh, he's very charming.

10:10.000 --> 10:11.000
He accepted without question.

10:11.000 --> 10:13.000
Oh, and naturally I'd like to meet him.

10:13.000 --> 10:17.000
That little disagreement we had last night wouldn't be anything compared to what your father would...

10:17.000 --> 10:18.000
Oh, don't worry about that.

10:18.000 --> 10:20.000
Dad won't be home until late tonight.

10:20.000 --> 10:21.000
Just come and enjoy yourself.

10:21.000 --> 10:24.000
Oh, and if you want to, bring some other girls along.

10:24.000 --> 10:25.000
All right, Margie, I will.

10:25.000 --> 10:28.000
Bye.

10:28.000 --> 10:29.000
Yeah?

10:29.000 --> 10:30.000
Oh, sure.

10:30.000 --> 10:32.000
You invited him just for Roberta.

10:32.000 --> 10:33.000
What?

10:33.000 --> 10:35.000
Well, I think you invited him for yourself.

10:35.000 --> 10:36.000
What's the matter with you?

10:36.000 --> 10:37.000
I thought you liked him.

10:37.000 --> 10:40.000
I like him fine up on the stage, but not around you.

10:40.000 --> 10:42.000
Who's a jealous stoop?

10:42.000 --> 10:49.000
Well, okay, goodbye.

10:49.000 --> 11:03.000
Now, Dad, what'll I do about him?

11:03.000 --> 11:04.000
Yes?

11:04.000 --> 11:05.000
My daughter?

11:05.000 --> 11:07.000
Oh, sure, put her on.

11:07.000 --> 11:09.000
Hi, dear, what's up?

11:09.000 --> 11:10.000
Mr. Horton?

11:10.000 --> 11:11.000
Why did he call there?

11:11.000 --> 11:13.000
He said he couldn't reach you at your office.

11:13.000 --> 11:16.000
You know how long-distance calls are sometimes.

11:16.000 --> 11:18.000
Anyway, he wants you to meet him at...

11:18.000 --> 11:20.000
Client or no client, this is ridiculous.

11:20.000 --> 11:21.000
What plane will he be on?

11:21.000 --> 11:23.000
You don't know?

11:23.000 --> 11:26.000
Well, there's a 610 plane, the 830 plane, the 1030 plane.

11:26.000 --> 11:28.000
All right, I'll meet all three of them.

11:28.000 --> 11:45.000
Thanks, honey.

11:45.000 --> 11:48.000
Angie, a piazza.

11:48.000 --> 11:50.000
So if you'd let me borrow your maid for a couple of hours,

11:50.000 --> 11:52.000
I'd really appreciate it, Miss Odette.

11:52.000 --> 11:55.000
Do you think I could get a peek at him, Angie?

11:55.000 --> 11:57.000
Certainly, you can join the party.

11:57.000 --> 11:58.000
You've got yourself a maid.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.000
Aw, thanks a million, Miss Odette.

12:00.000 --> 12:13.000
Send her over right away.

12:13.000 --> 12:16.000
Oh, excellent cocktail.

12:16.000 --> 12:17.000
Let me get you another.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.000
Thank you.

12:18.000 --> 12:21.000
I can't understand why our host hasn't spoken to me yet.

12:21.000 --> 12:22.000
A bit unusual, don't you think?

12:22.000 --> 12:23.000
Host?

12:23.000 --> 12:25.000
Yes, Angio Piazza.

12:25.000 --> 12:26.000
Who invited you, Miss Townsend?

12:26.000 --> 12:30.000
Oh, uh, Mr. Piazza, of course.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.000
Have you met the host yet?

12:31.000 --> 12:32.000
Host?

12:32.000 --> 12:33.000
You mean hostess, don't you?

12:33.000 --> 12:34.000
Morton Warnock.

12:34.000 --> 12:35.000
Miss Townsend.

12:35.000 --> 12:37.000
At least that's who invited me.

12:37.000 --> 12:39.000
Oh, excuse me, Morton.

12:39.000 --> 12:40.000
Of course.

12:40.000 --> 12:42.000
Shall we sit down?

12:42.000 --> 12:43.000
Mr. Warnock.

12:43.000 --> 12:44.000
Oh, Mr. Piazza.

12:44.000 --> 12:46.000
Delightful party.

12:46.000 --> 12:48.000
A charming friend of yours I was just chatting with.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.000
She's my friend?

12:49.000 --> 12:51.000
Well, of course, you have so many lady friends.

12:51.000 --> 12:55.000
I don't seem to recall the face, but the ankle looks slightly familiar, however.

12:55.000 --> 12:57.000
Delightful party, and I want to thank you for the...

12:57.000 --> 12:58.000
Oh, Mr. Warnock, you should not thank me.

12:58.000 --> 12:59.000
I should thank you.

12:59.000 --> 13:00.000
After all, you're the one who...

13:00.000 --> 13:02.000
Your drink, Mr. Warnock.

13:02.000 --> 13:03.000
Thank you.

13:03.000 --> 13:06.000
Suppose we ask the young lady, should the guest thank the host or the host thank the guest?

13:06.000 --> 13:07.000
Well, I say I should thank you.

13:07.000 --> 13:08.000
Ridiculous, Warnock.

13:08.000 --> 13:09.000
I should thank you.

13:09.000 --> 13:11.000
Such charming, gracious gentlemen.

13:11.000 --> 13:13.000
Suppose we give you both your way.

13:13.000 --> 13:14.000
Together now, say thanks.

13:14.000 --> 13:15.000
Splendid.

13:15.000 --> 13:16.000
Oh, indeed.

13:16.000 --> 13:17.000
Together.

13:17.000 --> 13:19.000
Thank you.

13:19.000 --> 13:20.000
I'm going to steal, Mr. Piazza.

13:20.000 --> 13:22.000
Mr. Warnock, do you mind?

13:22.000 --> 13:24.000
No, but I'd much rather if you'd steal, Mr. Warnock.

13:24.000 --> 13:26.000
But you go right ahead.

13:26.000 --> 13:27.000
Shall we go out on the balcony?

13:27.000 --> 13:28.000
I want to talk...

13:28.000 --> 13:30.000
I'll be right back.

13:30.000 --> 13:32.000
Excuse me.

13:32.000 --> 13:33.000
Who's the young lady?

13:33.000 --> 13:34.000
Why, don't you know her?

13:34.000 --> 13:35.000
No.

13:35.000 --> 13:36.000
Who is she?

13:36.000 --> 13:40.000
I don't know.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.000
Excuse me, miss.

13:41.000 --> 13:43.000
I'm an old friend of Mr. Piazza's.

13:43.000 --> 13:45.000
He said it would be all right if I dropped by.

13:45.000 --> 13:47.000
That all right with you, miss?

13:47.000 --> 13:48.000
Jones is the name.

13:48.000 --> 13:51.000
Sam Jones, an old-timer in the theatrical business.

13:51.000 --> 13:53.000
Freddy Wilson, go home.

13:53.000 --> 13:56.000
Well, if you really invited that guy for Roberta, why should I go home?

13:56.000 --> 13:57.000
All right.

13:57.000 --> 13:59.000
But don't you dare mess things up for me.

13:59.000 --> 14:02.000
I've got to get him alone and sell him on Roberta.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.000
Go on in.

14:03.000 --> 14:06.000
I'll see who this is.

14:06.000 --> 14:08.000
Miss Odette.

14:08.000 --> 14:09.000
Where is it?

14:09.000 --> 14:15.000
In the living room.

14:15.000 --> 14:20.000
What?

14:20.000 --> 14:22.000
I'll introduce you.

14:22.000 --> 14:25.000
Mr. Warnock, Mr. Piazza, may I present Miss Odette?

14:25.000 --> 14:26.000
Sure, what do you do?

14:26.000 --> 14:28.000
I'm Joe Piazza.

14:28.000 --> 14:29.000
Oh, my dear.

14:29.000 --> 14:30.000
Oh.

14:30.000 --> 14:31.000
There we are.

14:31.000 --> 14:33.000
Now, maybe we can get that fresh air.

14:33.000 --> 14:43.000
Of course.

14:43.000 --> 14:46.000
Oh, hi, Roberta.

14:46.000 --> 14:47.000
Freddy.

14:47.000 --> 14:51.000
Yeah.

14:51.000 --> 14:53.000
You say you want to talk to me about a woman.

14:53.000 --> 14:55.000
You have chosen my favorite subject.

14:55.000 --> 14:58.000
Well, this woman, she thinks you're wonderful.

14:58.000 --> 14:59.000
Thank you so much.

14:59.000 --> 15:01.000
Tell me more about this woman.

15:01.000 --> 15:07.000
Well, she's very mature, very warm, and just the right age.

15:07.000 --> 15:08.000
Mellow.

15:08.000 --> 15:11.000
Possessing an understanding one acquires only with experience.

15:11.000 --> 15:13.000
I think I understand what you mean.

15:13.000 --> 15:15.000
One that you know can't cook, but you don't care.

15:15.000 --> 15:17.000
Oh, but she can cook.

15:17.000 --> 15:19.000
Oh, please, Mr. Piazza, you've just got to be.

15:19.000 --> 15:20.000
Please call me Angio.

15:20.000 --> 15:22.000
All right, Angio.

15:22.000 --> 15:23.000
And what is your name?

15:23.000 --> 15:24.000
Margie.

15:24.000 --> 15:25.000
Margie Albright.

15:25.000 --> 15:26.000
Margie.

15:26.000 --> 15:28.000
To say that I'm intrigued is putting it mildly.

15:28.000 --> 15:31.000
Suppose you come to my apartment tomorrow night at 6 for dinner.

15:31.000 --> 15:33.000
We discuss the matter more thoroughly.

15:33.000 --> 15:35.000
You want me to come to your apartment?

15:35.000 --> 15:38.000
The Sky Tower Arms apartment, 1200.

15:38.000 --> 15:39.000
Well, all right.

15:39.000 --> 15:44.000
But I was hoping you'd want to do something about it right now.

15:44.000 --> 15:46.000
Tomorrow at 6.

15:46.000 --> 16:04.000
I promise I shall disappoint you then.

16:04.000 --> 16:05.000
Dad?

16:05.000 --> 16:09.000
Yeah, it's me.

16:09.000 --> 16:10.000
Where have you been?

16:10.000 --> 16:11.000
What are you, a joker?

16:11.000 --> 16:15.000
I went down to that darn airport and I've met every flying contraption that's ever been built.

16:15.000 --> 16:16.000
Oh, yes, the airport.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.000
Mr. Horton never showed up.

16:18.000 --> 16:21.000
Client or no client, I don't care how big a client he is.

16:21.000 --> 16:23.000
I'm going to call him right now and tell him off.

16:23.000 --> 16:24.000
It wasn't Mr. Horton's fault.

16:24.000 --> 16:25.000
It was my fault.

16:25.000 --> 16:26.000
Your fault?

16:26.000 --> 16:28.000
He called back right after I called you.

16:28.000 --> 16:30.000
He said to tell you he'd changed his plans.

16:30.000 --> 16:31.000
He wasn't going to come.

16:31.000 --> 16:33.000
He said to.

16:33.000 --> 16:35.000
And why didn't you call me?

16:35.000 --> 16:36.000
I forgot.

16:36.000 --> 16:37.000
You forgot.

16:37.000 --> 16:38.000
You forgot.

16:38.000 --> 16:42.000
And I've been waiting out there all this time and you just forgot.

16:42.000 --> 16:44.000
I think I'll go to bed before you get angry.

16:44.000 --> 16:45.000
Get angry?

16:45.000 --> 16:47.000
What do you think I am now?

16:47.000 --> 16:49.000
Dad, there's something else I want you to know.

16:49.000 --> 16:51.000
Everything I do is for your own good.

16:51.000 --> 16:53.000
I'd do anything to see you happy.

16:53.000 --> 16:56.000
Like not calling and letting me go to the airport?

16:56.000 --> 16:59.000
Well, even that was a big favor, only you don't realize it at the moment.

16:59.000 --> 17:02.000
I'd even lie if I thought it was for your own good.

17:02.000 --> 17:06.000
Remember that, just in case you find out that I may be told a little fib somewhere along the line.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.000
Oh, I get it.

17:07.000 --> 17:09.000
Your conscience is bothering you, eh?

17:09.000 --> 17:12.000
Margie, I'd a matter know what you're talking about.

17:12.000 --> 17:13.000
I've said all I'm going to say.

17:13.000 --> 17:15.000
Margie, come back here!

17:15.000 --> 17:16.000
Margie.

17:16.000 --> 17:18.000
I'm past 21 and you can't bop me around.

17:18.000 --> 17:20.000
As far as I'm concerned, you're still a child.

17:20.000 --> 17:21.000
I'm not a child.

17:21.000 --> 17:22.000
You're a child, you're going to do as I say.

17:22.000 --> 17:23.000
Now tell me what...

17:23.000 --> 17:24.000
I'm not a child.

17:24.000 --> 17:26.000
I know you're 21, but to me you're still a little girl.

17:26.000 --> 17:28.000
Little girl, huh?

17:28.000 --> 17:32.000
I suppose you think a little girl can have a date with a man like Angiopiasa.

17:32.000 --> 17:33.000
Stop being ridiculous.

17:33.000 --> 17:34.000
Ridiculous, huh?

17:34.000 --> 17:35.000
Well, guess this.

17:35.000 --> 17:40.000
This little immature girl, this little ungrown up child is having dinner with Angiopiasa

17:40.000 --> 17:43.000
at his apartment tomorrow night.

17:48.000 --> 17:51.000
A date with Angiopiasa.

17:51.000 --> 17:53.000
Could it be possible?

18:03.000 --> 18:05.000
Oh, Mr. Arbite.

18:05.000 --> 18:06.000
I was just bursting with pride.

18:06.000 --> 18:07.000
I'm looking for Margie.

18:07.000 --> 18:08.000
I just came home from the office.

18:08.000 --> 18:11.000
Oh, dear, little thing was probably so excited she forgot to tell you.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.000
She left just a few minutes ago.

18:13.000 --> 18:14.000
Left?

18:14.000 --> 18:15.000
For where?

18:15.000 --> 18:16.000
For Mr. Piazza's apartment.

18:16.000 --> 18:18.000
Angiopiasa?

18:18.000 --> 18:19.000
Yes.

18:19.000 --> 18:21.000
Goodness, you miss everything.

18:21.000 --> 18:24.000
He was in your apartment yesterday afternoon.

18:24.000 --> 18:25.000
What?

18:25.000 --> 18:26.000
Did she say where he lived?

18:26.000 --> 18:29.000
I believe Margie said the Sky Tower Arms.

18:32.000 --> 18:34.000
You should at least telephone.

18:34.000 --> 18:38.000
It's very annoying to have unexpected guests drop in on you for dinner.

18:39.000 --> 18:43.000
Oh, don't you know, she has a date with Angiopiasa.

18:43.000 --> 18:47.000
Yeah, I knew about that date, but I didn't think Margie would go through with it.

18:47.000 --> 19:08.000
Oh, I do hope Mr. Piazza has some extra canned goods on hand.

19:08.000 --> 19:10.000
The boy will be here with dinner in a moment.

19:10.000 --> 19:11.000
Oh, fine.

19:11.000 --> 19:17.000
White, soft and lovely as the pale winter moon, yet warm and fragrant as a tropical night.

19:17.000 --> 19:19.000
That's awful corny, but it knocks me out.

19:20.000 --> 19:22.000
I'm a right-handed smoker.

19:22.000 --> 19:23.000
May I?

19:23.000 --> 19:25.000
Oh, yes, of course, my dear.

19:25.000 --> 19:28.000
You know, I've been thinking quite a bit about that lovely lady you spoke of last evening.

19:28.000 --> 19:29.000
Yes?

19:29.000 --> 19:32.000
I'm sure that she and I could get along together splendidly.

19:32.000 --> 19:34.000
Oh, but I've hardly told you anything about her.

19:34.000 --> 19:36.000
Are you like me, my way?

19:36.000 --> 19:37.000
Your way?

19:37.000 --> 19:38.000
I originated it.

19:38.000 --> 19:39.000
I will show you.

19:39.000 --> 19:49.000
Now, suppose we try without the cigarette.

19:49.000 --> 19:51.000
But how could we without cigarettes?

19:51.000 --> 19:52.000
Hey!

19:52.000 --> 19:54.000
Why do you push me away, Margie, dear?

19:54.000 --> 19:55.000
Why did you kiss me?

19:55.000 --> 20:00.000
Well, why not stop all this nonsense and admit with a kiss, with your heart and soul, that you are the woman?

20:00.000 --> 20:01.000
What woman?

20:01.000 --> 20:02.000
The woman who's crazy about me.

20:02.000 --> 20:10.000
Holy mackerel!

20:10.000 --> 20:14.000
Hey, fella, loan me your jacket and let me take that card in and I'll give you ten bucks.

20:14.000 --> 20:15.000
I'm way ahead of you.

20:15.000 --> 20:16.000
Mr. Albright!

20:16.000 --> 20:18.000
Yes, and I don't need any help.

20:18.000 --> 20:19.000
I'll handle it.

20:19.000 --> 20:21.000
You've got to believe me, Mr. Piazza.

20:21.000 --> 20:22.000
Angio.

20:22.000 --> 20:23.000
I didn't mean me.

20:23.000 --> 20:25.000
Margie, I understand you are timid.

20:25.000 --> 20:28.000
That is why you didn't come out and say it was you from the start.

20:28.000 --> 20:33.000
Our dinner, a few glasses of champagne, some food, you will not be so shy.

20:33.000 --> 20:35.000
I know something else I won't be.

20:35.000 --> 20:37.000
I won't be here because I'm leaving.

20:37.000 --> 20:38.000
Well, you're acting like a little girl.

20:38.000 --> 20:39.000
Little girl?

20:39.000 --> 20:42.000
You ought to be ashamed of yourself, luring me up here.

20:42.000 --> 20:43.000
Goodbye.

20:43.000 --> 20:44.000
Margie!

20:44.000 --> 20:52.000
Margie, dear!

20:52.000 --> 20:53.000
Angio, darling.

20:53.000 --> 20:55.000
Unchangeable as a woman.

20:55.000 --> 20:56.000
Hold me.

20:56.000 --> 20:59.000
Till the end of time, till the well runs dry.

20:59.000 --> 21:00.000
Till the waiter leaves.

21:00.000 --> 21:01.000
Tick!

21:01.000 --> 21:04.000
Oh, Margie, as you say, you knock me out.

21:04.000 --> 21:06.000
All right, boy, you may serve.

21:06.000 --> 21:09.000
Margie, I'm going to say something to you I have never said to any other girl.

21:09.000 --> 21:10.000
What is it, Angio?

21:10.000 --> 21:13.000
I think, I think I could really fall for you.

21:13.000 --> 21:16.000
And you've never said that to any other girl?

21:16.000 --> 21:19.000
If I'm lying, may there never be another sunrise.

21:19.000 --> 21:22.000
It's going to be a long night tonight.

21:22.000 --> 21:23.000
Did anyone speak to you?

21:23.000 --> 21:24.000
Oh, I'm sorry, sir.

21:24.000 --> 21:25.000
No offense, sir.

21:25.000 --> 21:30.000
You know, I could spend the rest of my life here with you.

21:30.000 --> 21:32.000
May I have your autograph, Mr. Piazza?

21:32.000 --> 21:35.000
You're getting on my nerves, you know that?

21:35.000 --> 21:36.000
Just wanted your autograph.

21:36.000 --> 21:37.000
You could put it on my cuff.

21:37.000 --> 21:39.000
I'll be the envy of the commissary.

21:39.000 --> 21:40.000
Later, please.

21:40.000 --> 21:41.000
Later!

21:41.000 --> 21:45.000
You have lovely teeth.

21:45.000 --> 21:46.000
So white.

21:46.000 --> 21:48.000
Hey, speaking of teeth, look at mine.

21:48.000 --> 21:55.000
People ask me why that's so white, but you see, it's only an effect.

21:55.000 --> 21:57.000
I have a dark mouth.

21:57.000 --> 22:04.000
Say some more of those lovely things to me, Angie, dear.

22:04.000 --> 22:07.000
Margie, words fail to express my feeling for you.

22:07.000 --> 22:09.000
Let this be my messenger.

22:09.000 --> 22:12.000
Get out of here.

22:12.000 --> 22:13.000
I'll serve dinner myself.

22:13.000 --> 22:14.000
I'm sorry, sir.

22:14.000 --> 22:15.000
Union rules.

22:15.000 --> 22:16.000
I brought in the wagon.

22:16.000 --> 22:17.000
I got to serve.

22:17.000 --> 22:20.000
Doesn't the union have rules about your making a distance of yourself?

22:20.000 --> 22:21.000
Yes, sir.

22:21.000 --> 22:24.000
That's why when I serve, nobody even knows I'm around.

22:24.000 --> 22:25.000
Serve the champagne!

22:25.000 --> 22:26.000
Yes, sir.

22:26.000 --> 22:27.000
That's what I'm doing.

22:27.000 --> 22:33.000
May I propose a toast to the most charming young lady I have ever met.

22:33.000 --> 22:35.000
This is milk.

22:35.000 --> 22:37.000
Why did you serve the young lady milk?

22:37.000 --> 22:39.000
I'm not getting into any trouble serving minors.

22:39.000 --> 22:40.000
How do I know she's 21?

22:40.000 --> 22:41.000
If you've got likeness or something...

22:41.000 --> 22:42.000
Get out.

22:42.000 --> 22:43.000
Don't go by her apartment.

22:43.000 --> 22:45.000
I rang, but I guess nobody heard me.

22:45.000 --> 22:47.000
I'm here to fix the phone.

22:47.000 --> 22:49.000
Margie, I'm sorry for all these interruptions.

22:49.000 --> 22:51.000
I'll get rid of these people just a moment.

22:51.000 --> 22:52.000
Don't touch me.

22:52.000 --> 22:54.000
Margie, just a moment ago you...

22:54.000 --> 22:55.000
I'm leaving.

22:55.000 --> 22:56.000
Margie, dear.

22:56.000 --> 22:58.000
Vern Albright, what are you doing here?

22:58.000 --> 23:00.000
I don't have to do any guessing as to why you're here.

23:00.000 --> 23:03.000
Well, I have a perfectly good reason for being here, but I don't have to explain it to you.

23:03.000 --> 23:05.000
Well, the question is, what am I doing here?

23:05.000 --> 23:06.000
I'm taking my daughter home.

23:06.000 --> 23:07.000
Your daughter?

23:07.000 --> 23:08.000
And my girlfriend.

23:08.000 --> 23:11.000
Get out of my apartment, all of you.

23:11.000 --> 23:13.000
You can't push my father.

23:13.000 --> 23:16.000
Get out of my apartment.

23:16.000 --> 23:18.000
Being as you were having so much company, Mr. Piazza,

23:18.000 --> 23:25.000
I thought it wouldn't dice if I stopped at the store and brought you some groceries.

23:25.000 --> 23:28.000
I'm sorry I made such a fool of myself when I saw you there.

23:28.000 --> 23:30.000
Well, I suppose it did look suspicious.

23:30.000 --> 23:33.000
But how were you to know that I was there for the same reason as you and Freddy?

23:33.000 --> 23:35.000
We have our little differences, all of us.

23:35.000 --> 23:38.000
But we do stick together.

23:38.000 --> 23:40.000
I'm glad you didn't really go for that character.

23:40.000 --> 23:42.000
He kissed my hand.

23:42.000 --> 23:43.000
Which one?

23:43.000 --> 23:44.000
This one.

23:44.000 --> 23:46.000
Go wash it.

23:46.000 --> 23:52.000
And now, ladies and gentlemen, may I present a most gracious substitute for your regular host on the hour of symphonic charm,

23:52.000 --> 23:54.000
the romantic Angio Piazza.

23:54.000 --> 24:12.000
Applause

25:24.000 --> 25:34.000
Applause

